            "In (a) and (b), the baselines including the base VLM and \\naive Ensemble fail to understand the intention of the question (\\textit{kind of dog} and \\textit{native to north america}).\n",
            "While the text-only model understands the question better and suggests plausible answer candidates (\\textit{pug} and \\textit{wolf}), it has no access to the visual inputs and ultimately outputs an incorrect answer.\n",
            "On the other hand, \\modelname sensibly combines commonsense reasoning and visual context.\n",
